

========== 環境: docker.io/library/almalinux@sha256:e6d31b01fca10ed4f914e84e1139c3a40d6acf3d8346224a32f3e5649b1a3f7d ==========

$ cat /etc/almalinux-release
AlmaLinux release 8.10 (Cerulean Leopard)

$ dnf -y -q --setopt=install_weak_deps=False --setopt=tsflags= install rsyslog chrony man-db > /dev/null 2>&1; echo "dnf: exit=$?"
dnf: exit=0

$ dnf -y -q --setopt=install_weak_deps=False --setopt=tsflags= install mailx > /dev/null 2>&1 || dnf -y -q --setopt=install_weak_deps=False --setopt=tsflags= install s-nail > /dev/null 2>&1; echo "dnf: exit=$?"
dnf: exit=0

$ rpm -q rsyslog chrony; rpm -qf /usr/bin/mailx
rsyslog-8.2102.0-15.el8_10.1.x86_64
chrony-4.5-2.el8_10.x86_64
mailx-12.5-30.el8_10.x86_64


========== 第4章: 一般のログは /var/log/messages。起動時のメッセージは /var/log/boot.log ==========

$ grep -E '/var/log/(messages|secure|maillog|cron|boot\.log)' /etc/rsyslog.conf
*.info;mail.none;authpriv.none;cron.none                /var/log/messages
authpriv.*                                              /var/log/secure
mail.*                                                  -/var/log/maillog
cron.*                                                  /var/log/cron
local7.*                                                /var/log/boot.log


========== 第3章: chrony の設定ファイルとサービス名 ==========

$ ls -l /etc/chrony.conf
-rw-r--r-- 1 root root 1088 Nov  5  2024 /etc/chrony.conf

$ grep -E '^(pool|server) ' /etc/chrony.conf
pool 2.almalinux.pool.ntp.org iburst

$ ls /usr/lib/systemd/system/ | grep -E '^chrony'
chrony-dnssrv@.service
chrony-dnssrv@.timer
chrony-wait.service
chronyd.service


========== 第7章: mailx の -S（変数=値）で送り先の SMTP サーバーを渡す ==========

$ man mailx 2>/dev/null | grep -A4 -E '^ +-S '
       -S variable[=value]
              Sets  the  internal  option  variable  and,  in case of a string
              option, assigns value to it.  Note, that when setting from vari-
              able,  domain  name of host is automatically added if value does
              not contain any.  If you want to enter from address with owner's

$ man mailx 2>/dev/null | grep -A4 -E '^ +(smtp|mta)( |$)'
       smtp   Normally,  mailx  invokes  sendmail(8) directly to transfer mes-
              sages.  If the smtp variable is set, a SMTP  connection  to  the
              server  specified by the value of this variable is used instead.
              If the SMTP server does not use the standard port,  a  value  of
              server:port can be given, with port as a name or as a number.

$ echo x | mailx -S smtp=smtp://127.0.0.1:25 -s test root@localhost; echo "exit=$?"
exit=0
could not connect: Connection refused
. . . message not sent.


